          "phrases": [
            {"target": "Bonjour, comment allez-vous ?", "en": "Hello, how are you (formal)?"},
            {"target": "Ça va bien, merci. Et vous ?", "en": "I'm well, thanks. And you?"},
            {"target": "Salut ! À demain.", "en": "Hi! See you tomorrow."},
            {"target": "Pardon, je ne comprends pas.", "en": "Sorry, I don't understand."},
            {"target": "Merci beaucoup, madame.", "en": "Thank you very much, ma'am."}
          ],
          "grammar_note": "French has two 'you': tu (informal/singular) and vous (formal/plural). Use vous with strangers, elders, shopkeepers, and work colleagues. Tu is for peers, family, children, and close friends. Defaulting to vous is safer than defaulting to tu.",
