          "grammar_note": "French uses 'avoir' (to have) for age — literally 'I have 20 years', not 'I am 20'. The word 'ans' is required; dropping it ('J'ai vingt' on its own) is wrong. The final consonants of cinq, six, huit, dix are pronounced when the number stands alone or before a vowel, but go silent before a consonant: 'six ans' → 'siz-an', but 'six livres' → 'si livres'.",
